  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of Health, Protection and Food Assistance to Vulnerable Populations in Venezuela</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Amidst a continuing COVID-19 pandemic in 2021, IOM will contribute to the food security, health and protection as these are the most urgent and most-needed sectors for humanitarian assistance in Venezuela. IOM is targeting vulnerable populations in-country, individuals returning to Venezuela, and those in pendular migration. The Zulia state is benefitting from food security interventions, while the Sucre state benefits from both health and food security activities. Protection actions will, on the other hand, have a national focus. Particular attention is given to women and girls as they are the most vulnerable to food insecurity and protection risks.</narrative>
  </description>
